      "evidence": "scripts/rollout_alarm.py run_gh: `raise AlarmError(f\"gh {' '.join(args[:2])} failed: ...\")`. tests/test_rollout_alarm.py test_unreadable_run_fails_the_alarm asserts only the text \"gh api --paginate failed\".",
      "id": "alarm-delivery-error-names-weak-operation",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The spec requires the alarm job to exit non-zero 'naming the failed operation'. `run_gh` builds its message from only the first two gh args, so most failures read as `gh api --paginate failed: ...`, `gh issue create failed: ...` or `gh issue comment failed: ...`. Reading jobs and reading annotations both produce the same `gh api --paginate failed` text, and the endpoint is not named. This is weaker than the spec but still identifies the gh subcommand."
    }
